<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49145" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρῐαμβ-εύω</span></b> , pf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεθριάμβευκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					34
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρίαμβος</span>):—<i>triumph</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				6.53.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Posidon.
				1
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pomp.</u>
				45
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπό τινος</span>
			<i>triumph over</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Rom.</u>
				25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Gall.</u>
				1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ τῆς πατρίδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cor.</u>
					35
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				1.80
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τινι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4.31
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἐπὶ νίκῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
					3.9.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ μάχης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Publ.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. νίκην ἄδακρυν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.318b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεύτερον θρίαμβον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fab.</u>
					23
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>lead in triumph</i>, of conquered enemies, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Comp.Thes.Rom.</u>
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Col.</u>
				2.15
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εύεσθαι ὑπό τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cor.</u>
					35
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδ᾽ ἐν ἐμοὶ περιίδῃς -εύομενον
					σεαυτόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					84
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>lead in triumph</i>, as a general does his army, metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμᾶς ἐν Χριστῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>2 Ep.Cor.</u>
					2.14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>divulge, noise abroad</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξεφοίτα</span>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
